  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final S2 removes any automatic sales stop above 5%, leaves per-model rates open to customers on request without public publication, and has no sunset on the over-limit allowance, which favours Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%). S5 sets a mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 with no transition or interim trigger, which bites on Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9), and S3's six-year retrofit window matches Northwind's red line and suits its 38% shut-off coverage. S1 is strong (24-hour reporting covering all thermal incidents, which closes the unreported-incident gap for both companies), and S4 sets built-in suppression at 36 months, which suits Halcyon's cost position."
 },
